cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Nous: a persistent epistemic substrate for grounding language models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wikström
    given-names: Björn
repository-code: "https://github.com/base76-research-lab/Nous"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
abstract: >
  Nous is a research prototype testing whether a language model becomes more
  reliable when it can consult a persistent, structured record of what is
  known before speaking — typed relations with graded confidence, tracked
  contradictions, and explicit boundaries around what is not known. As of the
  release date above, no complete, independently scored benchmark run
  demonstrates a reliability improvement over a bare model; see
  eval/RESULTS_INDEX.md in the repository for the current evidence status.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The Larynx Problem: Why Large Language Models Are Not Artificial Intelligence"
  authors:
    - family-names: Wikström
      given-names: Björn
  year: 2026
  url: "https://zenodo.org/records/19413234"
